// ----- EXACT decimal expansion of a double ---------------------------------
//
// strconv.FormatFloat prints the EXACT value of the double and rounds HALF TO
// EVEN, which the naive `Math.floor(a * 10^prec + 0.5)` gets wrong twice over:
// it rounds half AWAY from zero (Go's %.0f of 2.5 is "2", not "3") and it loses
// every digit past 2^53 ("%f" of 1e100 has to print all 101 of them). Both were
// measured on the differential probe.
//
// A finite double is m * 2^e with m an integer below 2^53, so its exact decimal
// is a bignum: for e >= 0 it is m doubled e times, and for e < 0 it is m
// multiplied by 5 exactly -e times with the point placed -e digits from the
// right (because 2^-e == 5^-e / 10^-e). The bignum is a little-endian array of
// base-10000 limbs; multiplying by 2 or by 5 keeps every intermediate under
// 50000 + 10000, which a double holds exactly.

