// rt.pyGenericAlias (jsrt.go:8662): the memoized list[int]-style alias of a
// type object. Keyed by the origin's NAME and the rendered parameter, so the
// same written alias is the same value twice and `type X = list[int]` compares
// equal.
//
// NOT EXACT in one place, and it cannot be: Go recovers a closure's name from
// rt.pyFuncNames, the side table js_pyfnname fills, which lives in another
// chunk of this file. The name is read back through the prelude's pyGetAttr,
// whose "__name__" arm reads that same table (jsrt.go:9134) - the same answer
// by a different route, and the __name arm of a class object below is Go's
// literally.
function pyCGenericAlias(origin, param) {
